  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Suppose that $\\triangle ABC$ has vertices at $A(-1,1)$, $B(0,4)$ and $C(3,3)$. Prove that $\\triangle ABC$ has a right angle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\angle ABC=90^\\circ$.\n\nThe gradients of $AB$ and $BC$ are $3$ and $-\\frac13$; their product is $-1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{4-1}{0-(-1)}\\\\m_{AB}&=3\\\\m_{BC}&=\\frac{3-4}{3-0}\\\\m_{BC}&=-\\frac13\\\\m_{AB}m_{BC}&=3\\left(-\\frac13\\right)\\\\m_{AB}m_{BC}&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $AB\\perp BC$, so $\\angle ABC=90^\\circ$ and $\\triangle ABC$ has a right angle.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
